expeditions/2026-06-25-theta-components/threads/03-theta-h1-h2/codex/order-vs-components-stdout.log:564:2026:Clearly, Theorem \ref{thm:UsingAvoidingIdeal} is less computationally efficient than our earlier theorems calculating $C$ and $\theta$. Nevertheless, it (just like Theorem \ref{thm:Pseries}) also displays the a priori non-obvious fact that $C$ and $\theta$ are invariant under the permutation of the components of $\ud$ (cf.~Corollary~\ref{cor:PermutationInvariance}). 
